Root cause:
The bug was caused by the driver not supporting the new revisions (v1.1 and v1.2) of the IQS7222D device, which have different memory maps compared to previous versions. This lack of support would lead to incorrect handling of device operations and potentially result in malfunctioning input processing.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
.prod_num = IQS7222_PROD_NUM_D,
.fw_major = 1,
.fw_minor = 0,
```
Reason:
The driver was only configured to support the original version (v1.0) of the IQS7222D device, which does not account for the new revisions (v1.1 and v1.2) that have different memory maps. This lack of support would lead to incorrect handling of device operations, resulting in malfunctioning input processing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
.fw_major = 1,
.fw_minor = 1,
```
```c
.fw_major = 1,
.fw_minor = 2,
```
Reason:
By adding support for the new firmware major and minor versions (1.1 and 1.2), the driver is now able to correctly interpret the different memory maps associated with these revisions. This ensures proper handling of device operations and resolves the malfunctioning input processing issue.


